  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Addition of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in dilute and cold solution gives a solution, prussian&nbsp;blue solution&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>The reaction is as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>]</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>KCl</mi></math></p>"
